Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:57:28 -0000
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: cancel departing BSS timeouts

Removing an AP BSS can free its callback context or replace the driver's
first BSS while scan and rfkill timeouts still refer to the old context.
Those callbacks must not run after the BSS has been torn down.

Cancel the departing BSS scan timeout in wpa_driver_nl80211_if_remove().
Also cancel the driver-context rfkill timeout when drv->ctx belongs to
that BSS, before first-BSS reassignment or BSS destruction. Leave a
surviving BSS's rfkill timeout alone when its context differs.

This carries the independent timeout cleanup from the alternative 027
without changing 027's borrower-removal or driver-lifetime policy.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
index a1bd55de1ea4..612e8aaf243b 100644
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -9105,6 +9105,10 @@ static int wpa_driver_nl80211_if_remove(struct i802_bss *bss,
 	}
 
 	bss->in_deinit = 1;
+	eloop_cancel_timeout(wpa_driver_nl80211_scan_timeout, drv, bss->ctx);
+	if (drv->ctx == bss->ctx)
+		eloop_cancel_timeout(wpa_driver_nl80211_send_rfkill, drv, drv->ctx);
+
 	if (bss != drv->first_bss) {
 		struct i802_bss *tbss;
 
